$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A 0.12-0.23 M DMF solution of bromopyrazines
(1) containing 2 mol% Pd[P(C6H5)3]4, 2.5 equivalents of
diisopropylethylamine and 3.0-4.5 equivalents of LiCl was heated at 120
°C for 10 min to 6 h under nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was
treated as described in the Table 1. A 0.18-0.29 M DMF solution of
bromopyrazines (1) containing 2 mol% Pd[P(C6H5)3]4 was heated at 120 °C
for 1.5-24 h under nitrogen atmosphere. To the reaction mixture was added
saturated aqueous KF solution and stirred at room temperature for
overnight. The solution was diluted with CH2Cl2 and extracted with CH2Cl2
The organic layer was concentrated to dryness after filtration and the
crude mixture was separated on a silica gel column to yield 2. Table 2,
yield 86%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5- and 3,5-substituted 2-aminopyrazines by Pd mediated
Stille coupling
