$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
3-ethyl-3-[6-(4-thiophen-2-yl-phenyl)-hexyloxymethyl]-oxetane 32 To 31
(305 mg, 1.41 mmol.) and 2-(tributylstannyl)-thiophene (385 mg, 1.2 eq.)
was added 10mL dry PhMe, previously degassed with 3 x freeze/thaw/pump
cycles (Ar). The mixture was stirred under Ar until dissolution of the
starting materials was observed, then bubbled with Ar for 20 min. The
mixture was then heated to reflux, and Pd(PPh3)4 (46 mg, 5 mol.%) in dry,
degassed PhMe (5 mL) was added via cannula. The reaction mixture was
stirred at reflux under Ar for 18 h. Once cool, the reaction mixture was
filtered through Celite, and the solvent removed in vacuo. The crude oil
was purified via column chromatography (4:1 petroleum ether 40-60 °C:
EtOAc), yielding the title compound as clear oil (266 mg, 86 %). Rf =
0.68 (3:1 petroleum ether 40-60 °C: EtOAc). 1H NMR δ = 7.52 (d, 2H, 3J =
8.2 Hz), 7.27 (dd, 1H, 3J = 3.7 Hz, 4J = 1.2 Hz), 7.24 (dd, 1H, 3J = 3.7
Hz, 4J = 1.2 Hz), 7.18 (d, 2H, 3J = 8.2 Hz) 7.07 (dd, 1H, 3J = 5 Hz, 3.7
Hz), 4.45 (d, 2H, 2J = 5.8 Hz), 4.38 (d, 2H, 2J = 5.8 Hz), 3.52 (s, 2H),
3.44 (t, 2H, 3J = 6.4 Hz), 2.62 (t, 2H, 3J = 7.6 Hz), 1.74 (q, 2H, 3J =
7.3 Hz), 1.68-1.51 (m, 4H), 1.43-1.32 (m, 4H), 0.88 (t, 3H, 3J = 7.3 Hz).
13C NMR δ = 144.55, 142.19, 131.89, 128.88, 127.89, 125.85, 124.25,
122.55, 78.57, 73.39, 71.53, 60.35, 43.40, 35.54, 31.31, 29.03, 28.21,
26.77, 26.03, 21.00, 17.40, 14.18, 13.59, 8.20. MS (EI+) m/z = 358
([M]+., 74 %), 359 ([M+1]+., 18 %). HRMS (EI+) = 358.196175, C22H30O2S
requires 358.196652. IR (oil, cm-1) = 2928, 2856, 1536, 1502, 1459, 1433,
1414, 1375, 1288, 1210, 1114, 1050, 979, 850, 814, 692, 635, 600.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
