$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5,5'-(azulene-4,7-diyl)bis(3-dodecylthiophene) (7a) was prepared from
4,7-dibromoazulene (4a) and 4-dodecyl-2-trimethyltinthiophene (6a). A 5
mL glass vial was charged with a stirrer bar, 0.2 mmol of azulene 4a, 0.5
mmol of 6a, Pd2(dba)3 (4 mol% Pd), P(o-tol)3 (8 mol%) and chlorobenzene
(2 mL). The glass vial was purged with nitrogen and securely sealed. The
glass vial was placed into a microwave reactor and heated at 150 °C for
45 minutes with stirring. After cooling to room temperature, the solvent
was evaporated and the crude oligomer was purified using column
chromatography. 86% yield. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CD2Cl2, ppm): δ 8.72 (1H, d,
J = 2 Hz), 7.92 (1H, dd, J 1 = 11 Hz, J 2 = 2 Hz), 7.84 (1H, t, J = 4
Hz), 7.64 (1H, d, J = 3 Hz), 7.47 (1H, dd, J 1 = 4 Hz, J 2 = 1 Hz), 7.43
(1H, d, J = 2 Hz), 7.37 (1H, d, J = 11 Hz), 7.28 (1H, d, J = 2 Hz), 7.11
(1H, d, J = 1 Hz), 6.93 (1H, d, J = 1 Hz), 2.69 (2H, t, J = 8 Hz), 2.64
(2H, t, J = 8 Hz), 1.73 - 1.65 (4H, m), 1.42 - 1.28 (36H, m), 0.88 (6H,
t, J = 7 Hz). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ 145.9, 144.2, 143.5,
143.0, 140.6, 139.6, 136.6, 135.4, 134.7, 132.7, 129.3, 127.1, 124.7,
124.6, 120.9, 120.6, 119.4, 118.2, 31.2, 29.92, 29.86, 29.81, 29.77,
28.99, 28.97, 28.95, 28.92, 28.91, 28.8, 28.7, 28.6, 22.0, 13.2. HRMS
(FI) (m/z): (M)+ calcd for C42H60S2 628.4136; found, 628.4113.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stimuli-Responsive Azulene-Based Conjugated Oligomers with
Polyaniline-like Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
