$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Cross-Coupling
Reaction Using Ligand 4 (Procedure B). In a glove box, the Schlenk tube
equipped with a stir bar was charged with Pd2(dba)3 (11.2 mg, 0.012 mmol,
1.5 mol %), CsF (272 mg, 1.8 mmol), and ligand 4 (11 mg, 0.025 mmol, 3.5
mol %). The tube was fitted with a rubber septum and removed out of the
glove box. One mL of 1,4-dioxane, aryl chloride (1.0 equiv, aryl chloride
if solid was added inside the glove box), and organotin reagent (1.1
equiv) were added successively using syringes. The tube was sealed with a
Teflon screwcap. The reaction mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at room
temperature then heated with stirring at the indicated temperature for
the indicated time. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature,
diluted with ether or acetone, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
2,5-Dimethylbiphenyl12 (Table 3, entry 2). Procedure B was followed using
2-chloro-p-xylene (116 mg, 0.816 mmol), phenyltributyltin (0.30 ml, 0.898
mmol), and 4 (12.7 mg, 0.029 mmol, 3.5 mol %). The reaction mixture was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (hexanes) to afford 127
mg (85%) of the desired product as a colorless liquid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
room temperature coupling of aryl bromides, coupling of aryl triflates,
and synthesis of sterically hindered biaryls
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
