$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Cross-Coupling
reaction Using Ligand 1 (Procedure A). In a glove box, the Schlenk tube
equipped with a stir bar was charged with Pd2(dba)3 (11.2 mg, 0.012 mmol,
1.5 mol %) CsF (272 mg, 1.8 mmol). The tube was fitted with a rubber
septum and removed out of the glove box. One mL of 1,4-dioxane, stock
solution of ligand 1 in dioxane (16.8 mg, 0.049 mmol, 6 mol %), aryl
chloride (1.0 equiv, aryl chloride if solid was added inside the glove
box), and organotin reagent (1.1 equiv) were added successively using
syringes. The tube was sealed with a Teflon screwcap. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at room temperature then heated with
stirring at the indicated temperature for the indicated time. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, diluted with ether or
acetone, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel. 2-Phenylpyridine (Table
1, entry 5). Procedure A was followed using 2-chloropyridine (94 mg,
0.816 mmol) and phenyltributyltin (0.30 mL, 0.898 mmol). The reaction
mixture was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (10% ethyl
acetate/hexanes) to afford 108 mg (85%) of the desired product as a light
yellow liquid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
room temperature coupling of aryl bromides, coupling of aryl triflates,
and synthesis of sterically hindered biaryls
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
