$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
4-[(2R,3R)-3-(benzyloxymethyl)-1-tritylaziridin-2-yl]-benzoate (6). Aryl
Halide As Limiting Reagent, Preparative Scale. In a 100 mL, oven-dried,
single-neck round bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar
and a rubber septum were placed crude aziridinyl stannatrane 8 (0.56 g,
0.85 mmol estimated by NMR assay), methyl 4-iodobenzoate (5, 0.147 g,
0.563 mmol), CuDPP (0.24 g, 0.85 mmol) and Pd(tBu3P)2 (0.014 g, 0.003
mmol) inside the glovebox. This mixture was flushed with a stream of N2
and dissolved in dry DMF (50 mL). The resulting solution was stirred at
rt with monitoring for completion of reaction (4 h). The reaction mixture
was diluted with ethyl acetate (100 mL) and water (100 mL). The layers
were separated and the organic layer was washed with water (3 × 20 mL),
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. Silica gel chromatography (10% ethyl
acetate in hexanes) afforded 6 as oil, identified by NMR comparison with
the reported data.1a. Aziridinyl Stannatrane 8 as Limiting Reagent,
Preparative Scale. In a similar procedure, aziridinyl stannatrane 8 (0.56
g, 0.85 mmol), methyl 4-iodobenzoate (5, 0.33 g, 1.27 mmol), CuDPP (0.24
g, 0.85 mmol) and Pd(tBu3P)2 (0.032 g, 0.063 mmol) were combined as
before and stirred at rt (4 h). The same workup and purification afforded
6 as oil having the same spectroscopic characteristics. 0.39 g (85%),
clear oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Stille reaction, gove box
used, small scale, optimization study (based on copper source, solvent,
time and temperature)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stille Coupling of an Aziridinyl Stannatrane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Theddu, Naresh; Vedejs, Edwin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(10), 5061-5066

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME182 STEP1
