$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for Substituted
Quinolizinum Salts 23-26. Method A. A flame-dried two-necked flask was
charged under argon with the corresponding bromoquinolizinium salts 4-7
(50 mg, 0.173 mmol) in dry DMF (2 mL). Then 10 mol% CuI (3 mg, 0.0173
mmol), 5 mol% Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 0.0086 mmol) and the corresponding
stannane (0.225 mmol) were slowly added. After stirring at room
temperature (15-20 h) or heating at 60-80 ºC as indicated, the solution
was filtered through a small pad of Celite and washed with methanol. The
solution was concentrated and the solid isolated by filtration. Some
coupling products obtained from bromoquinoliziniums 4 and 5 were isolated
as picrates (TNP) by treatment of the crude bromide with a slight excess
of sodium picrate in refluxing ethanol for 1 h. Other derivatives were
isolated as hexafluorophosphates by treatment with ammonium
hexafluorophosphate in water followed by purification by column
chromatography on silica gel, using CH2Cl2/MeOH (9.5:0.5) as the eluent.
For the coupling products obtained from 3- and 4-bromoquinolizinium
salts, after washing with methanol, the solvent was removed and the
residue was triturated with ether and EtOAc. Purification of the crude
product by column chromatography on silica gel (reverse phase) using
H2O/AcOH (100:0.5) as the eluent yielded the coupling products 25 and 26,
which were isolated as bromides. 4-(2-Thiophenyl)quinolizinium Bromide
(26d): Following procedure A, from 7 and tributyl-2-thiophenylstannane
(0.449 mmol, 167 mg), after stirring at rt for 22 h, 86 mg (85%) of 26d
were isolated as a brown solid; mp 161-163ºC; IR (KBr) νmax 3112, 2952,
1618, 1455, 808 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CD3OD) δ 9.34 (d, 1H, J = 7.1Hz);
8.65 (t, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz); 8.43(dd, 2H, J = 6.4, 14.1 Hz); 8.15 (d, 1H, J
= 4.1 Hz); 8.07-8.02(m, 2H); 7.72(dd, 1H, J = 1.1, 3.7 Hz); 7.45(dd, 1H,
J = 3.7, 5.1 Hz). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CD3OD) δ 145.8,141.4, 138.3, 137.2,
134.8, 133.6, 132.6, 131.9, 129.7, 129.4, 128.9, 125.5. MS (ESI+) m/z 212
(M+). Calcd for C13H10NSBr: C, 53.42; H, 3.42; N, 4.79; S, 10.96. Found:
C, 53.26; H, 3.65; N, 4.52; S, 10.75.
