$DATUM Methyl 4-[(2R,3R)-3-(benzyloxymethyl)-1-tritylaziridin-2-yl]-benzoate
(6). Aryl Halide As Limiting Reagent, Preparative Scale. In a 100 mL,
oven-dried, single-neck round bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic
stirring bar and a rubber septum were placed crude aziridinyl stannatrane
8 (0.56 g, 0.85 mmol estimated by NMR assay), methyl 4-iodobenzoate (5,
0.147 g, 0.563 mmol), CuDPP (0.24 g, 0.85 mmol) and Pd(tBu3P)2 (0.014 g,
0.003 mmol) inside the glovebox. This mixture was flushed with a stream
of N2 and dissolved in dry DMF (50 mL). The resulting solution was
stirred at rt with monitoring for completion of reaction (4 h). The
reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (100 mL) and water (100
mL). The layers were separated and the organic layer was washed with
water (3 × 20 mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. Silica gel
chromatography (10% ethyl acetate in hexanes) afforded 6 as oil,
identified by NMR comparison with the reported data.1a. 0.24 g (80%),
clear oil. [α]20D = -70.0 (c 1.1, CHCl3); HRMS-ES+ (m/z) [M + H] calcd
for C37H34NO3, 540.2539, found 540.2535; IR (neat, cm-1) 3020, 1725; 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, ppm) δ 8.01 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (d, J = 8.5
Hz, 2H), 7.49 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 6H), 7.29-7.16 (m, 13H), 6.90 (dd, J = 7.5
Hz, 2.5 Hz, 2H), 4.18 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (d, J = 12. 0 Hz, 1H),
3.96 (s, 3H), 3.85 (dd, J = 10.1, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 3.36 (dd, J = 10.2, 8.0
Hz, 1H), 2.54 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 1.95 (ddd, J = 7.7, 6.5, 4.3 Hz, 1H).
13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3, ppm) δ 167.1, 143.9, 142.8, 137.8, 129.5,
129.3, 128.2, 128.0, 127.9, 127.5, 127.3, 126.8, 75.4, 72.8, 66.9, 52.1,
39.1, 38.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Stille reaction, gove box
used, optimization study (based on copper source, solvent and
temperature), scalable (preparative, gram scale)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stille Coupling of an Aziridinyl Stannatrane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Theddu, Naresh; Vedejs, Edwin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(10), 5061-5066

