$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromide 17. CuCl (5.99 g, 16.66 mmol), LiCl (3.21 g, 75.7 mmol) and
Pd(PPh3)4 (1.59 g, 1.51 mmol) were combined under N2 in a round bottom
flask. This mixture was added in one portion to a solution of TIPSalcohol
15 (8.62 g, 15.14 mmol) and stannane 16 (8.71 g, 15.55 mmol) in dry,
degassed DMSO (150 mL). The reaction was stirred at rt for 30 min, and
poured carefully onto saturated NaHCO3 (300 mL). The resultant slurry was
diluted with ether (300 mL) and filtered through celite, rinsing
thoroughly with ether. The organic phase of the resultant filtrate was
separated, and the aqueous phase extracted with ether (3 x 200 mL). The
combined organic layers were then dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated.
Purification by silica-gel chromatography (ethyl acetate-hexane, 1 : 10)
gave bromide 17 (9.17 g, 85%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 0.98 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 9 H), 1.04 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 9 H), 1.08-1.16 (m, 3
H), 1.27- 1.39 (m, 1 H), 1.43-1.55 (m, 1 H), 1.92-2.01 (m, 2 H),
2.02-2.10 (m, 2 H), 2.34 (s, 3 H), 4.23 (s, 3 H), 4.89 (ddt, J = 10.2,
2.0, 1.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.96 (ddt, J = 17.1, 2.0, 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 5.40 (t, J =
7.1 Hz, 1 H), 5.75 (ddt, J = 17.1, 10.2, 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.25 (d, J = 7.4
Hz, 2 H), 7.33 (td, J = 8.1, 1.1 Hz, 1 H), 7.39 (td, J = 7.3, 1.3 Hz, 1
H), 7.87 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2 H), 8.02 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 8.57 (s, 1 H),
9.09 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 12.3, 17.9, 18.0,
21.5, 24.2, 33.7, 37.9, 54.9, 71.7, 112.9, 114.5, 116.1, 123.9, 125.0,
125.2, 127.0, 128.8, 129.3, 130.0, 134.8, 135.1, 137.2, 138.6, 145.2,
147.6, 154.6; IR (neat) 2943, 2865, 1640, 1535 cm-1; HRMS (M+H+) calcd
for C35H47N3O4SSiBr 712.2240, found 712.2249.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Strategy for the Total Synthesis of Dragmacidin E. Construction of the
Core Ring System
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Huntley, Raymond J.; Funk, Raymond L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(21), 4775-4778

