$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (10) Typical Procedure: a mixture of 1 (442 mg, 1 mmol),
1-iodonaphthalene (2b, 279 mg, 1.1 mmol), Pd2dba3 (23 mg, 0.05 equiv of
Pd) and AsPh3 (31 mg, 0.10 mmol) in DMF (4 mL) was purged with N2 for 10
min at room temperature and stirred under N2 at 60 °C for 2.5 h. The
reaction mixture was then diluted with water and extracted with ether.
The organic phase was washed twice with water, dried (Na2SO4) and
evaporated. Chromatography of the residue (525 mg) on silica gel (21 g)
using CH2Cl2/AcOEt = 99/1 as eluent gave 3b. 345 mg (85%). mp 100-101 °C;
[α]D22 +45° (c 1.0, CHCl3) [lit.41 mp 100-102 °C; [α]D20 +48.16° (c 1.0,
CHCl3)]; IR (CHCl3) 3437, 1741, 1709, 1499, 1368, 1167 cm-1; 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.44 (9H, s, t-Bu), 3.12 (1H, dd, J = 14.1, 6.1 Hz, CHH),
3.23 (1H, dd, J = 14.1, 5.4 Hz, CHH), 3.77 (3H, s, CO2Me), 4.68 (1H, m,
α-CH), 5.09 (1H, d, J = 7.4 Hz, NH), 7.24-7.91 (11H, m, ArH).
