$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acylation of Bromopyrazines, 1,2-Bromopyridine (6) and Bromobenzenes;
General Procedure. A mixture of the corresponding hetaryl or aryl
bromides (0.50 mmol), PdCl2(Ph3P)2 (18 mg, 0.026 mmol, 5 mol%) and 95%
CuI (15 mg, 0.075 mmol, 15 mol%) in anhyd MeCN (4.0 mL) was placed under
argon, and tributyl(1-ethoxyvinyl)tin (2;12 0.54 g, 1.5 mmol) or
tributyl(1-ethoxyprop-1-enyl)tin (4;1 0.56 g, 1.5 mmol) was introduced by
a syringe. After heating for the time given in Tables 1-3, 1.5 M aq HCl
(20 mL) was added to quench the reaction. The solution was refluxed for 1
h, neutralized with NaHCO3 and extracted with EtOAc (3 15 mL). The
combined extracts were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced
pressure. To the residue was added sat. KF-MeOH13 (3 mL), and the mixture
was filtered. After removal of the solvent, the residue was
chromatographed on Silica Gel 60 (hexane-EtOAc, 4:1-15:1) to provide the
acyl compounds. 2-Acetyl-5-phenylpyrazine (3a). Colorless needles, yield
85%. Mp 161.5-162°C (EtOH). IR (KBr): ν = 1692 (C=O), 1364, 1285, 1018,
749, 693 cm-1. 1H NMR (270 MHz): δ = 2.75 (s, 3H), 7.51-7.59 (m, 3H),
8.07- 8.12 (m, 2H), 9.06 (d, 1H, J = 1.5 Hz), 9.26 (d, 1H, J = 1.5 Hz).
13C NMR (67.8 MHz): δ = 25.9, 127.4, 129.2, 130.8, 135.5, 140.5, 143.0,
145.7, 155.1, 199.1. MS: m/z (%) = 199 (MH+, 100). Anal. Calcd for
C12H10N2O: C, 72.71; H, 5.08; N, 14.13. Found: C, 72.47; H, 5.02; N,
14.10.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies on pyrazines; 38: acylation of bromopyrazines and 2-bromopyridine
via copper-cocatalytic Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sato, Nobuhiro; Narita, Nobuhiko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (10), 1551-1555

