$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM By Direct Zincation of Commercially Available Organolithium Reagents: A
solution of the commercially available organolithium compound (5.00 mmol)
was added at -78 °C to a solution of ZnCl2 (15.0 mL, 7.50 mmol, 0.5 M in
THF). The resulting mixture was stirred at r.t. for 30 min and was then
added via a syringe to a solution of 2,4-dibromothiazole (1; 486 mg, 2.00
mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (46.0 mg, 0.10 mmol), and dppf (56.0 mg, 0.10 mmol) in
THF (10 mL). After stirring for 16 h at r.t., the reaction was quenched
with sat. aq NH4Cl (10 mL), and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O
(3 x 20 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (20 mL).
After drying (Na2SO4) and filtration, the solvent was removed and the
residue was purified by flash chromatography over silica gel
(pentane-Et2O, 30:1-20:1). 4-Bromo-2-butylthiazole (4a), yield 375 mg,
1.70 mmol, 85%. 1H NMR (360 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.91 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3 H,
CH3), 1.38 (virt. sext, J ≈ 7.5 Hz, 2 H, CH2), 1.73 (virt. quint, J ≈ 7.6
Hz, 2 H, CH2), 2.96 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2 H, ArCH2), 7.03 (s, 1 H, ArH). 13C
NMR (90 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 13.6 (q, CH3), 22.1 (t, CH2), 31.8 (t, CH2),
33.2 (t, CH2), 115.5 (d, CarH), 124.1 (s, CarBr), 172.7 (s, Car).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Negishi cross-coupling (2nd stage)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2,4-Disubstituted thiazoles by regioselective cross-coupling or
bromine-magnesium exchange reactions of 2,4-dibromothiazole
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gross, Stefan; Heuser, Stefan; Ammer, Carolin; Heckmann, Golo; Bach,
Thorsten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (2), 199-206

