$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 3,3-Diarylacrylonitriles : General Procedure for the
Synthesis of 3,3-Diarylacrylonitriles by the Stille Cross-Coupling
Reaction of 3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)acrylonitrile with
Aromatic Iodides or Bromides. A mixture of
(Z)-3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)acrylonitrile or
(E)-3-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)-acrylonitrile, (0.1 mmol,
1.0 equiv), aryl halide (1.20 equiv), cesium fluoride (2.20 equiv), and
Pd(dppf) (5.0 mol %) or Pd2(dba)3 (2.5 mol%) and PtBu3 (5.0 mol%) in
anhydrous DMF (1.0 mL, degassed by freeze-pump-thaw-pump method) was
stirred in dark under argon at 60 °C for indicated time. The reaction
mixture was then cooled to room temperature and filtered a short column
of silica gel (5 g), and the column was washed with ethyl acetate. The
organic solution was concentrated on arotary evaporator under vacuum. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and purified by column
chromatography on SiO2 eluting with EtOAc-hexanes.
(E)-3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(3,5-dimethylphenyl)acrylonitrile, yellow
solid, yield 78 mg, 85%. mp 95-96 °C. IR (film) 2917, 2210, 1599, 1515,
1463, 1266, 1140, 1024, 806, 737 cm1; EIMS m/z 293 (M+, 100), 278 (10),
246 (20); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.09 (bs, 1 H), 7.02 (bs, 2 H),
6.88-6.78 (m, 3 H), 5.63 (s, 1 H), 3.91 (s, 3 H), 3.83 (s, 3 H), 2.34 (s,
6 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.1, 151.1, 148.8, 138.0, 137.1, 131.6
(2C), 127.3, 122.3, 118.4, 111.0, 110.7, 92.8, 56.0, 21.3; Anal. Calcd
for C19H19NO2: C, 77.79; H, 6.53; N, 4.77. Found: C, 77.81; H, 6.59; N,
4.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
