$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.7. General Experimental Procedure for Stille
Cross-Coupling Reaction. Aryl halide (3.0 mmol), tributylphenyltin (1.101
g, 3.0 mmol) and LiCl (0.381 g, 9.0 mmol) were added to 5 mL ethanol. To
this, 0.002 g of IRMOF-3-PI-Pd was added and the mixture was heated to a
temperature of 80 °C in an oil bath. Progress of the reaction was
monitored by GC at regular intervals. After completion of the reaction,
the solid catalyst was filtered and the filtrate was extracted four times
with dichloromethane (4 × 15 mL). The organic layers thus collected were
combined and washed with water and brine. The organic phase was then
dried over Na2SO4 and filtered and concentrated under vacuo. The crude
product was purified by column chromatography over silica gel (mesh
60−120) to obtain the corresponding product. Products were analyzed by GC
and/or 1H NMR measurement. All the products are known and reported in the
literature. 1H NMR data of these products were consistent with the
reported values. Table 3. Stille Cross-Coupling Reactions Catalyzed by
IRMOF-3-PI-Pda Biphenyl Table 4. Suzuki and Stille Coupling Reaction of
Aryl Halide with 4-Methylphenylboronic Acid and Triphenyltin,
Respectively, Catalyzed by IRMOF-3-PI-Pd Entry 3 p-nitrobiphenyl Yellow
solid, yield 84%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm): 8.32-8.29 (m, 2H),
7.76-7.73 (m, 2H), 7.65-7.61 (m,2H), 7.53-7.45 (m,3H); Anal. Calcd. for
C12H9NO2: C, 72.35%; H, 4.55%; N, 7.03%. Found: C, 72.37%; H, 4.56%; N,
7.01%.
