$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(2-Pyridyl)-2,2'-bithiophene (4) A mixture of
2-(2-bromothien-5-yl)pyridine 1 (2.4 g, 10 mmol),
2-(tributyltin)thiophene (4.1 g, 11 mmol) and [Pd(PPh3)4] (290 mg, 0.25
mmol) in dry DMF (70 ml) was de-aerated by bubbling argon through the
mixture for 10 min and then the reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at
115°C. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure on a rotary
evaporator and the residue recrystallised from petrol ether. Yield 84%.
5-(2-Pyridyl)-2,2'-bithiophene (4), Yield 84%. 1H NMR (270 MHz, CDCl3): δ
6.67 (dd, 1H, J 5.2, 3.7 Hz), 7.10-7.18 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.45
(d, 1H, J 3.7 Hz), 7.65 (m, 2H), 8.55 (ddd, 1H, J 5.4, 1.8, 1.1 Hz).
Anal. calcd. for C13H9NS2: C, 64.16; H, 3.73; N, 5.76. Found: C, 64.31;
H, 3.89; N, 5.51.
