$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille Reaction with Compounds 5; General
Procedure (Method A) To a stirred mixture of 5 (0.33 mmol), freshly
prepared Pd(PPh3)4 (30 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.08 equiv) and LiCl (35 mg, 0.82
mmol, 2.5 equiv) in anhyd DMF (3 mL) was added tributyl(1-ethoxyvinyl)tin
(160 mL, 0.49 mmol, 1.5 equiv). The mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 12 h
and then the solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The crude residue was
purified by flash chromatography (eluent indicated below) to give 6a-c.
8-Acetyl-4-(N-methyl-N-phenylamino)-2-methylsulfanylpyrazolo[
1,5-a]-1,3,5-triazine (6b) Chromatography eluent: PE, then
CH2Cl2-PE-EtOAc (5:6:1); yield: 84%; solid. Mp 223-225 °C (MeOH). IR
(KBr): 1670, 1560 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.59 (s, 3 H, CH3),
2.70 (s, 3 H, CH3), 3.75 (s, 3 H, CH3), 7.16-7.19 (m, 2 H, ArH),
7.38-7.45 (m, 3 H, ArH), 8.08 (s, 1 H, H-7). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
14.4 (CH3), 29.2 (CH3), 42.5 (CH3), 109.4 (C), 126.1 (2 CH), 127.6 (CH),
129.2 (2 CH), 144.1 (C), 145.4 (CH), 148.2 (C), 151.5 (C), 170.9 (C),
192.1 (C=O). MS (ESI): m/z = 314 (M + H)+. Anal. Calcd for C15H15N5OS: C,
57.49; H, 4.82; N, 22.35. Found: C, 57.32; H, 4.73; N, 22.55.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 8-substituted pyrazolo[1,5-a]-1,3,5-triazine derivatives by
palladium-catalyzed cross-coupling reactions
